  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "73 (a striving verse): the command is not glossed; only As-Sa'di's restriction «حيث اقتضت الحال الغلظة عليهم». Al-Muyassar's «بالسيف» is not used. Nothing drawn in 73. 74: their oath (1-4) is answered by the verse itself; «على أيدي المؤمنين» is not used. Two paths for «فإن يتوبوا… وإن يتولوا». STAGING v4: c1 (73) stays ambient: the striving verse, addressed to the Prophet himself (nothing drawn, background quiet). c2 (74): a town by day; two small groups of three men (the hypocrites). During their oath (74:1-4) nobody speaks (As-Sa'di: they swore to the Prophet, who is never shown; no speech toward an empty side). They do say the word of disbelief to each other on 74:6 and 74:9 (As-Sa'di: words said one after another). Their plot (74:12-15) is not acted (As-Sa'di: against the Prophet's life), and nothing is drawn for the enrichment (74:20-24: no giver may stand for the Prophet). The two-paths plate keeps the condition of 74:25-32 (repent or turn away) as a symbol; no gesture is acted inside the conditions, and nothing is drawn for the punishment."
